ling stations might call with jack-high or queen-high.\n\nBut safer to **check back and show down**.\n\nBecause:\n\n- If you bet, you get called by better hands (like AK, flush) and fold out worse (like KJ, K10).\n- So **negative expected value**.\n\nThus, **best action is to check (0)** and see showdown.\n\nGoing all-in would be overkill — you only have 19,200 chips, all-in would be huge bluff or value, but no clear value.\n\nFolding is silly — you have top pair.\n\nRaising risks losing more when behind, gains little when ahead.\n\nSo **checking is optimal**.\n\nReason:  \nYou have top pair with a strong kicker, and the opponent’s passive play on turn and river suggests weakness. Betting would likely only get calls from hands that beat you (like flushes or AK) and fold out worse. Checking allows you to realize equity and win at showdown if your hand is best.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
